# Environment for examples/docker-compose. Copy this file to .env, fill in
# the empty values, and never commit .env: it holds the database password
# and the cookie signing key (.gitignore in this directory lists it).
#
# Every variable the server requires is here, in the order server/app/config.go
# reads them; the optional ones are at the end, commented out with their
# defaults. The server refuses to start and names every missing or malformed
# variable at once, so a mistake here is one restart to fix, not several.

# --- Postgres -------------------------------------------------------------
# The same three values create the database in the postgres container and
# tell the server how to reach it. DATABASE_HOST and DATABASE_PORT are set
# in compose.yaml (the service name "db", port 5432) and a value for either
# here is ignored by the server container.
DATABASE_NAME=loop_sessions
DATABASE_USER=loop_sessions
# Any string; Postgres only ever sees it over the Compose network.
DATABASE_PASSWORD=change-me-before-first-boot

# --- Cookie signing key ---------------------------------------------------
# At least 32 random bytes, base64. Signs the dashboard's session cookie;
# rotating it signs everyone out. Generate one with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# and paste the output (one line, with its trailing "=" padding) after the
# equals sign. Left empty, the server refuses to start.
SESSION_KEY=

# --- Firebase (sign-in) ---------------------------------------------------
# Sign-in is Google accounts through a Firebase project; README.md,
# "The three Firebase values" says where each comes from.
#
# The project id (Firebase console, Project settings, General).
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=__PROJECT__
# The project's web API key (Firebase console, Project settings, General,
# "Web API Key"). Public by design (it is served to every browser on the
# sign-in page), but it is a project-specific value, so it is left empty
# here rather than guessed. Left empty, the server refuses to start.
FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to <FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID>.firebaseapp.com, which is right
# unless the project uses a custom auth domain.
#FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=

# --- Who may sign in ------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated mail domains. A Google account outside these domains is
# refused at sign-in whatever Firebase says about it; anyone on them is
# enrolled as a member automatically the first time they sign in, so this
# list is the access gate for members.
ALLOWED_DOMAINS=example.com
# The first admins, created at boot if missing (never changed afterwards;
# the People page promotes, disables and re-enables people from then on).
# Each address must be on ALLOWED_DOMAINS or the server refuses to start.
ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com

# --- Where the server is --------------------------------------------------
# The origin browsers use, with no path. compose.yaml binds the server to
# the loopback interface on port 8080, so this is the value for a laptop;
# behind TLS it becomes https://sessions.example.com. An http:// value
# turns off the cookie's Secure attribute, which is what loopback needs.
PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------
# The host port compose.yaml publishes. The container always listens on
# 8080 (compose.yaml fixes PORT for the server, so a PORT set here is
# ignored). Change PUBLIC_URL to match.
#HOST_PORT=8080
# Which published image tag to run, or what to stamp into a local build.
#SERVER_IMAGE_TAG=latest
#SERVER_VERSION=dev
# Log level: debug, info, warning, error.
#LOG_LEVEL=info
# Retention, in days; 0 keeps everything, which is the default. A window
# that is on must be at least 7 days, and bodies (transcripts) cannot
# outlive sessions (the rollup).
#RETENTION_BODY_DAYS=0
#RETENTION_SESSION_DAYS=0
# Domain pairs the analytics export treats as one Workspace.
#DOMAIN_ALIASES=example.com:example.org
# The derive runner: "HH-HH" in the server's timezone (default 02-06) or
# "always"; rows per second; rows per batch (250..5000).
#DERIVE_WINDOW=02-06
#DERIVE_ROWS_PER_SEC=
#DERIVE_ROWS_PER_BATCH=
# Slack mirroring; unset means no mirror at all.
#SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
#LOOP_SESSIONS_SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# A GCS bucket the daemon's self-upgrade reads from; unset serves no /dl.
#RELEASE_BUCKET=
